CONTEXT
Reference: https://recent.design/i/eo2zyqk-iridescent-home-button (design by Jakub Wuzik — video: https://cdn.recent.design/items/eo2zyqk/0/3000x3000.mp4). There is NO source code available for this — you must recreate the effect from scratch as a reusable component. Apply it to the navigation buttons of my portfolio (Next.js 15 / React 19 / TS / Tailwind v4 / Motion).

THE EFFECT (what to build)
A dark pill/circular button with a thin glowing iridescent ring traveling around its border — a rotating multi-hue gradient that lives on the border only, with a soft outer glow, animating continuously in a slow loop and intensifying on hover/press.

IMPLEMENTATION SPEC
1. Create <IridescentButton /> in components/ui/ — polymorphic (renders <Link> or <button>), accepts children, size (sm/md/icon), and className.
2. Layer structure:
   - Base: near-black surface (#111 on #090909), 1px rgba(255,255,255,.08) inner border, fully rounded (pill / circle for icon variant).
   - Ring: a rotating conic-gradient confined to a 1.5–2px border. Technique: pseudo-element with conic-gradient(from var(--angle), ...) + CSS mask (mask-composite: exclude with two backgrounds, or padding-box/border-box trick) so ONLY the ring shows the gradient.
   - Glow: a second identical pseudo-element behind it with filter: blur(8–12px) and reduced opacity — this creates the iridescent halo.
3. Animation: register the angle with @property --angle { syntax: '<angle>'; inherits: false; initial-value: 0deg; } and animate --angle 0→360deg. Do NOT animate transform:rotate on the pseudo-element (it distorts non-circular pills); animating the registered custom property keeps the gradient sweep correct on any shape. Duration ~4s linear infinite at rest.
4. States:
   - Rest: ring at low opacity (~0.35), glow nearly off (~0.15). Subtle, not loud.
   - Hover: ring and glow ramp to full over 300ms ease-out, rotation speeds up to ~2.5s, button lifts 1px (Motion spring, no bounce).
   - Press: scale 0.97 with a spring.
   - Focus-visible: same as hover + a 2px offset white outline for accessibility.
5. Gradient palette — MUST fit my design system (no loud RGB): desaturated iridescent hues, e.g. conic stops cycling through soft violet → cyan → warm white → soft violet, all at moderate saturation (think oil-slick / pearl, not rainbow). Expose the stops as CSS variables so I can tune them in one place.
6. prefers-reduced-motion: freeze the rotation (static gradient at a fixed angle), keep only opacity transitions.
7. Fallback: browsers without @property support (check via @supports) get a static gradient ring — no broken animation.

WHERE TO APPLY
